{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540329-ic-justification-for-raisimg-attributes","id":1540329,"title":"IC Justification for raisimg attributes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-13T22:04:22-07:00","id":1540329,"title":"IC Justification for raisimg attributes","content":"What attibutes will chness help with raising<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Aany ideas on difference between aan exercise that helps raiae stamina one which so aids in strength","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T08:15:09-07:00","id":1540358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540329-ic-justification-for-raisimg-attributes#post1540329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What attibutes will chness help with raising</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you meant Chess? If so i would go with intelligence as chess is mostly a game of memorisation and pattern recognition.<br /> I guess you could make an argument for raising wits attribute by focusing on the the blitz format.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540329-ic-justification-for-raisimg-attributes#post1540329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Aany ideas on difference between aan exercise that helps raiae stamina one which so aids in strength</div> </div> </div> </div>For Stamina anything that deals with endurance or cardio, training like boxing, running, biking, hiking, climbing, swimming, etc.<br /> <br /> For strength things that focus on power and weight lifting.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not a really sport oriented guy, but generally the rule for training is : Short and intense for strength and lengthy and repeated for endurance.<br /> <br /> A character could also raise attribute by getting a job that implies using those attribute. For example, a movers will most likely develop both strength and stamina as a result of carrying heavy furnitures all day long.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T09:10:01-07:00","id":1540360,"title":"","content":"In reality, we're not neatly divided into categories that make the game rules functional. There are lots of different types of physical &quot;strength&quot; in the fitness world that would translate differently between the physical Attributes; and even extend into things like mental traits (keeping up high level physical training regimens quickly becomes a strain on your mental endurance as well).<br /> <br /> The easiest guide for XP is... what have the players actually been using (not always rolling)? If a PC has been in a bunch of chases rolling Stamina, but also using Speed (including Str + Dex)? Let them increase whatever they're looking to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T22:12:54-07:00","id":1540497,"title":"","content":"oh ideas on a supernatural developing transhuman attributes?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> think even then chess will work for Intelligence but need pretty heavy weights for strength","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T08:45:30-07:00","id":1540510,"title":"","content":"For supernatural attributes, it really depends on the splat. Vampires, for example, wouldn't train strength by lifting, they would simply get mystically stronger by having a better mastery of their vitae, but i could see them getting more charismatic being doing charisma stuff (speeches, parties, etc). I'm not very well versed in the other splat to give you proper example.<br /> <br /> Now as far as developping transhuman attributes, which i assume you mean are attributes above 5, i'd simply go with feat that are superhuman in nature; Bench pressing cars, sprinting for a day, etc.<br /> <br /> For strength and stamina it's fairly easy to come up with ideas as they are roughly quantifiable, but mental and social ones are way too nebulous to come up with specific requirements.<br /> <br /> Thousand years of nights list some transhuman feat for every attribute.<ul><li><b>Intelligence:</b> Character can remember everything, Can solve the unsolvable. Can translate lost language. Can treat any diseases.</li> <li><b>Wits: </b>Character can discern any lie and has incredible reaction speed, so much that others think they can read the future.</li> <li><b>Resolve:</b> Can Meditate through an earthwquake and oppose the ''collective will of a nation''. Nearly immune to mental influence. Incredibly patient and focused.</li> <li><b>Strength:</b> Has the destructive strength of a speeding truck. Can rip heads with their bare hands.</li> <li><b>Dexterity:</b> Can perform brain surgery with a spatula. So quiet they can sneak on someone standing right in front of them. So graceful it's unsetling.</li> <li><b>Stamina:</b> Can run all night long, can withstand blizzard.</li> <li><b>Presence: </b>As charismatic as Jesus Christ. Even a casual glance can be enough to intimidate someone. Always the center of attention, even when they don't want.</li> <li><b>Manipulation: </b>Can manipulate a parent into abandonning their children willingly. Others will believe what they want.</li> <li><b>Composure: </b>Immune to temptation and influence.</li> </ul>Of course all of this is to take with a grain of salt, after all 6 dot of intelligence is only 1 dot above 5. Honestly, i'd go with want feels right for your chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T09:30:36-07:00","id":1540512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540329-ic-justification-for-raisimg-attributes?p=1540510#post1540510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thousand years of nights list some transhuman feat for every attribute.<ul><li><b>Intelligence:</b> Character can remember everything, Can solve the unsolvable. Can translate lost language. Can treat any diseases.</li> <li><b>Wits: </b>Character can discern any lie and has incredible reaction speed, so much that others think they can read the future.</li> <li><b>Resolve:</b> Can Meditate through an earthwquake and oppose the ''collective will of a nation''. Nearly immune to mental influence. Incredibly patient and focused.</li> <li><b>Strength:</b> Has the destructive strength of a speeding truck. Can rip heads with their bare hands.</li> <li><b>Dexterity:</b> Can perform brain surgery with a spatula. So quiet they can sneak on someone standing right in front of them. So graceful it's unsetling.</li> <li><b>Stamina:</b> Can run all night long, can withstand blizzard.</li> <li><b>Presence: </b>As charismatic as Jesus Christ. Even a casual glance can be enough to intimidate someone. Always the center of attention, even when they don't want.</li> <li><b>Manipulation: </b>Can manipulate a parent into abandonning their children willingly. Others will believe what they want.</li> <li><b>Composure: </b>Immune to temptation and influence.</li> </ul>Of course all of this is to take with a grain of salt, after all 6 dot of intelligence is only 1 dot above 5. Honestly, i'd go with want feels right for your chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other notable mechanics for transhuman Attributes are the optional Reversal Points rule introduced in Imperial Mysteries and the additional effects available to Deviant characters with the Superhuman [Attribute] Variation at a rating high enough to set their minimum dots in that Attribute to 6 or higher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T19:19:52-07:00","id":1540543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1540329-ic-justification-for-raisimg-attributes?p=1540497#post1540497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> oh ideas on a supernatural developing transhuman attributes?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> think even then chess will work for Intelligence but need pretty heavy weights for strength</div> </div> </div> </div>At that point the increase comes from their supernatural nature, not from mundane training. It's a sign of the character becoming something else, something outside the laws of nature.<br /> <br /> Vampires feel the blood changing and bringing its power to the dead body, its small muscles becoming able to exert a strength far above they have the right to do. If it comes from a muscle at all.<br /> <br /> Werewolves hunt and devour spirits linked to great strength, and as spirits made flesh, they start to manifest that same strength in this material world. A Mage finds out the Supernal symbol for strength and becomes one with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}